VERDICT: FAIL
CHECKER: checker-second
FAMILY: adversarial
TASK: IP1
ATTEMPT: 1
---

## Primary defect: §3.5 Compact period-context is NEVER wired to the Insights page

SPEC.md §3.5 states explicitly: "`insights.html` passes `Compact true`." The
"Claim under test" in the brief restates this: "(3.5) a Compact
period-context (no card chrome, stale note as a warning callout with
'Note:') on Insights ONLY." Acceptance criteria for IP1 require "Compact
period-context callout only when Stale, non-Compact output byte-identical to
master's" — this presupposes Compact is actually reachable on the real page.

Evidence this was never wired:

1. grep for every non-test occurrence of "Compact" in the branch tree:
   ```
   $ grep -rn "Compact" $BRANCH --include="*.go" --include="*.html" | grep -v "_test.go"
   web/templates/components/shared/period-context.html:3:{{if $.Compact}}<section class="space-y-2">{{else}}<section class="bg-white dark:bg-gray-800 rounded-lg shadow p-4">{{end}}
   web/templates/components/shared/period-context.html:4:    <p class="text-sm {{if $.Compact}}...
   web/templates/components/shared/period-context.html:6:    {{if $.Compact}}<p class="rounded-lg border border-warning bg-warning-soft ...
   ```
   Zero hits in any handler or in `insights.html` itself. The only place
   "Compact" ever appears with value `true` is inside
   `internal/templates/render_insights_ip1_test.go`, which renders the
   `shared/period-context` partial in ISOLATION via
   `renderer.RenderToString("shared/period-context", map[string]any{"Period": stale, "Compact": true})`
   — it never exercises the actual page template's invocation.

2. `web/templates/pages/insights.html:41` (the only call site inside the
   real page) is unchanged from a plain `.` pass-through:
   ```
   <div id="period-context">{{template "shared/period-context" .}}</div>
   ```
   Confirmed via diff against master — this line is byte-identical to
   master; the spec's required `(dict "Period" .Period "Compact" true)`
   invocation was never made.

3. `internal/handlers/insights/handlers.go:261-277` — `handleInsights`
   builds `pageData := map[string]interface{}{...}` (the `.` passed at
   call site 1) with keys Title/ActiveTab/Insights/Investigation/
   PaceVerdict/Period/StartDate/EndDate/MinDate/MaxDate/Preset/Anomalies/
   AnomalyTotal/PriceCreep/PriceCreepTotal — no `Compact` key. In Go
   templates a missing map key is the zero value, so `{{if $.Compact}}`
   evaluates false. Verified this Go template semantic directly:
   ```
   $ cat /tmp/tmpldemo.go
   ... t.Execute(os.Stdout, map[string]interface{}{"Title":"Insights"}) with {{if $.Compact}}COMPACT{{else}}NOTCOMPACT{{end}}
   $ go run /tmp/tmpldemo.go
   NOTCOMPACT
   ```

4. Built the branch (cp -a minus .git/data, `go build ./cmd/server`),
   served it against a copied `testdata/` on `:8099` (killed after test,
   confirmed down: `curl :8099/insights` -> exit/000 after kill), and
   fetched `/insights`:
   ```
   $ curl -s http://127.0.0.1:8099/insights?start=2024-12-31&end=2025-12-31 -o /tmp/ip1_insights.html
   $ sed -n '247,250p' /tmp/ip1_insights.html
       <div id="period-context">
   <section class="bg-white dark:bg-gray-800 rounded-lg shadow p-4">
       <p class="text-sm text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">Selected period: 2024-12-31 to 2025-12-31 (366 calendar days) · Latest transaction: 2025-12-31</p>
   ```
   The live rendered Insights page shows FULL CARD CHROME
   (`bg-white dark:bg-gray-800 rounded-lg shadow p-4`) — i.e. exactly
   master's non-Compact rendering, not the Compact "no card chrome"
   design the spec and the brief's claim require. §3.5 is unimplemented on
   the one page it was supposed to change; the partial-level unit tests
   (`TestIP1PeriodContextCompact`) pass because they test the partial in
   isolation and never catch the missing integration.

This is squarely in scope (§3.1–§3.6 named in the IP1 task row) and
directly contradicts the "Claim under test" and the worker's underlying
design intent. Default-to-FAIL is not even needed here — this is
unambiguous: grep, diff, a Go template semantics probe, and a live server
render all agree.

## Other adversarial checks run (informational — not overridden by the above)

- Money-figure diff (item 1): rendered `/insights` on master (:8098) and
