  strip's 3×(Monthly,Annual) tiles, verified character-for-character equal
  to their own group cards' figures later in the document (sanctioned
  exception, brief item 1):
  tile1 `$26.98`/`$323.76` == `Estimated monthly $26.98 · Estimated annual $323.76` (subscriptions);
  tile2 `$2,107.57`/`$25,290.83` == bills group card;
  tile3 `$323.08`/`$3,876.87` == other group card.
  One additional order effect observed: within a single price-creep
  finding `<li>`, the evidence-sentence figures now appear before the
  actual-transaction amount in document order (master: amount, meta,
  evidence; branch: link, chips, meta, evidence, amount, caption) — this
