## Observations (backlog, not a FAIL basis)
- Evidence-sentence-before-amount document-order swap in findings rows
  (see item 1 above) — cosmetic, approved by §3.3's two-column layout,
  not a figure-value defect.
- `investigation.go`'s `add()` still passes `a.Severity+" severity"` as the
  `Evidence` field for anomaly rows even though the template only ever
  reads `.Evidence` inside `{{with .Creep}}` (nil for anomalies, so it's
  dead data, never rendered) — harmless but worth a follow-up cleanup so
  the field isn't misleading to a future reader.
